# AI Workflow & Code Quality

## Code Generation
- Don't generate boilerplate in bulk
- Create only what's necessary for the current change
- Keep suggestions concise; prefer one-sentence definitions when introducing a concept

## Documentation
- Maintain docs/ with architecture notes, ADRs, PUBLIC_API, and test strategy
- Provide a `make docs` task
- When AI proposes a design, also propose an ADR stub with trade-offs and alternatives

## Code Standards
- Treat AI as a design/docs/test assistant
- AI output is pseudo-code to be rewritten, not production code
- Never include secrets/credentials
- Respect .gitignore, .llmignore, and repo policies
- Use British English in comments, docs, commit messages, and PR text